# Optional TURN relay for WebRTC NAT traversal.
#
# When unset, the app is STUN-only and cross-network joins can fail with a
# "Couldn't reach your friend's game" timeout (strict/symmetric NAT, UDP-blocking
# firewalls). A TURN relay provides a guaranteed fallback path.
#
# Copy this file to .env for local `npm run dev` testing. For production, set the
# same three vars in the Vercel project's Environment Variables (they are inlined
# at build time, so a redeploy is required after changing them).
#
# VITE_TURN_URL may be a comma-separated list (plain UDP + a TLS/443 fallback).
# The values below are Metered Open Relay — free, no signup, best-effort. Swap in
# dedicated credentials if you need reliability for real users.

VITE_TURN_URL=turn:openrelay.metered.ca:80,turns:openrelay.metered.ca:443?transport=tcp
VITE_TURN_USERNAME=openrelayproject
VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=openrelayproject
